          %h2#scope Scope
          %p
            %strong Differential geometry
            is a mathematical discipline studying geometry of spaces using differential and integral calculus. Classical differential geometry studied submanifolds (curves, surfaces…) in Euclidean spaces. The traditional objects of differential geometry are finite and infinite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable manifolds
            modelled locally on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+topology"} differential topology
          %h2#generalized_smooth_spaces_from_pov
            Generalized smooth spaces from
            = succeed "POV" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
          %p
            Finite-dimensional differential geometry is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            modeled on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            between them.
          %p
            Formally, it is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} geometry
            modeled on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pregeometry+%28for+structured+%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes%29"} pre-geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} =
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
          %p
            This includes a sequence of concepts of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                (see there for details) is a locally
                = succeed "-representable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi CartSp
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi CartSp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(CartSp)
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
                (see there) is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete sheaf
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi CartSp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(CartSp)
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
                is a locally representable object in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-sheaf"} (2,1)-sheaf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-topos"} (2,1)-topos
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Sh
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi CartSp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(CartSp)
            %li
              %p
                an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
                is an object in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-sheaf (∞,1)-topos
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Sh
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi CartSp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(CartSp)
          %p
            Similarly, standard models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            are modeled on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pregeometry+%28for+structured+%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes%29"} pre-geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} =
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ThCartSp"} ThCartSp
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ThCartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(ThCartSp)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topos
            called the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers+topos"} Cahiers topos
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimal space
                is a certain object in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ThCartSp
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ThCartSp
            %li
              %p
                an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid"} ∞-Lie algebroid
                is a certain object in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Sh
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ThCartSp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(ThCartSp)
